{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SigmaJGeometricCarrier","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.shadow_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.shadow_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L97-L117","doc":"**Shadow assembly (the composed conditional theorem at the degenerate\nlocus).** For ANY Hodge assignment `f` satisfying the B1 dictionary\n(normalization + ρ-intertwining) and ANY ρ-symmetric weight `w`:\n(1) `f` agrees with the FORCED `hodgeShadow` on the whole pair\n    (`shadow_unique`, PR #3960 — the dictionary has no freedom), and\n(2) the KL eigenvalue at `q = 1` times the selected channel's weight equals\n    the pair total — the q→1 one-loop restores the doubled unit, bean B4's\n    target statement read at the shadow level.\nThe hypotheses are exactly the shadow content of the open B2 lift; they are\nexplicit binders, not axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.channel_share_is_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.channel_share_is_half","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L90-L95","doc":"**The selected channel carries exactly half the doubled total.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.rho_forced_equal_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.rho_forced_equal_split","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**ρ-forced equal split.** Any weight symmetric under the reality\ninvolution assigns equal weight to the two members of the degenerate pair —\nthe shadow of: reality of the Laplacian forces every spectral trace to split\nequally across `H^{1,0} ⊕ H^{0,1}` (B4b V2/V3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.conj_I_eq_neg_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.conj_I_eq_neg_I","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L77-L78","doc":"ρ exchanges the degenerate pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.pairCount_ne_bettiOneBring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.pairCount_ne_bettiOneBring","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L72-L75","doc":"The ½ is the conjugate-PAIR share, not `1/b₁`: the pair count is not the\nBring Betti number (the `1/(π·b₁) = 1/(8π)` coincidence is a different\ndecomposition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.kl_eigenvalue_at_one_eq_pairCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.kl_eigenvalue_at_one_eq_pairCount","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The tower's own KL eigenvalue at the classical point equals the\nconjugate-pair count: the q→1 one-loop restores the doubled total. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.bettiOneBring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.bettiOneBring","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L65-L66","doc":"`b₁(Bring) = 2g = 8` — recorded to disambiguate, never to divide by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.klEigenvalueAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.klEigenvalueAtOne","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The `q = 1` value of the KL eigenvalue `[2]_q` of `b_s = σ + q⁻¹` on the\nsymmetric channel (B4a: the one-loop coefficient is −[2]_q·x exactly). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.pairCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.pairCount","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly.lean#L57-L59","doc":"The conjugate-pair count — the shadow of `dim {H^{1,0}, H^{0,1}} = 2`\n(the #3920 Hodge doubling). ","signatureChunk":0}]}